## Name of the node
-name bondy@127.0.0.1

## No Cookie as we do not want distributed erlang but Partisan


## Explicit connections only.
-connect_all false
-hidden

## The erts flags that used to live here — +sbwt, +c, +C, +P, +A, +zdbbl — are
## now set in bondy.conf and emitted into the generated args file loaded below.
## Keeping copies here was worse than redundant: the generated file is loaded
## last and a duplicated erts + flag resolves to the last occurrence, so these
## lines could not win, and +A 64 was in fact losing to the schema's default of
## 1. +K was also removed: it is absent from the erts 16.4 usage output, and both
## `+K true` and `+K false` leave erlang:system_info(kernel_poll) at true, so
## kernel polling is unconditional and the flag does nothing.


## Finally load the remaining vm.args that are generated by cuttlefish from the
## input provided in the bondy.conf file
-args_file etc/generated/vm.generated.args
-args_file etc/vm.extra.args